Answer concisely.<|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>In Classic the Voidwalker is the first pet you learn and the one you keep out when you're not actively questing.

Succubus is better DPS/CC for solo questing, but she is swapped in for pulls and dismissed afterwards. The Voidwalker is left out in towns / while travelling because Torment/Suffering gives free threat/taunt, Consume Shadows gives out-of-combat regen, and Sacrifice gives a free shield, and it's the big, intimidating default pet most warlocks never bother to dismiss. [end of text]


